Note for ~/.config/plasmanotifyrc
=================================

After hand-editing plasmanotifyrc, run:

    systemctl --user restart plasma-plasmashell.service

plasmashell watches its config through KConfigWatcher, which reloads only on the
org.kde.kconfig.notify D-Bus signal - not on filesystem changes. A plain text
edit sends no such signal, so the new value is ignored until plasmashell is
restarted. Changing the setting through System Settings instead writes the file
*and* emits the signal, so it applies live.

This note lives outside plasmanotifyrc because KConfig's INI backend skips '#'
lines when parsing and rewrites the file from its in-memory entry map, so any
comment there is dropped the next time plasmashell saves (which happens whenever
a new app sends its first notification and gains a Seen=true entry).

Current setting: [Notifications] PopupPosition=TopRight
